===Etymology===
Alteration of earlier {{etyl|enm}} ''[[wlappen#Middle English|wlappen]]'' "to wrap, fold" from {{etyl|ang}} *''wlappan, wlæppan, wlappian, wlæppian'' from {{proto|Germanic|wrappan-, wlappan-|to wrap, fold|lang=ang}} from {{proto|Indo-European|werb-|to bend, turn|lang=}}. Akin to {{etyl|enm|-}} ''[[wrappen#Middle English|wrappen]]'' "to wrap", {{etyl|dan|-}} ''[[vravle]]'' "to wind", Old {{etyl|ita|-}} ''[[goluppare]]'' "to wrap" (from {{etyl|gem}}). More at [[envelop]].

===Verb===
{{infl|enm|verb}}

# to [[wrap]], [[fold]]

